      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `Printer.Pretty.addHead()` throws `IllegalArgumentException` when called with a negative depth value (which causes `StringUtil.padding()` to receive a negative width). Let me write an improved version.Now I'll write the improved test with better variable names and a clear explanation of the test's intent.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version uses descriptive variable names (`rootTextNode`, `fileWriter`, `output`, `prettyPrinter`, `bodyElement`) and a Javadoc comment that explains why `addHead(-1)` triggers the `IllegalArgumentException`, making the test's intent immediately clear without changing any runtime behaviour."
